# A widget of several clauses applied, above the line that gives it, to the late plain
# result of a widget of one clause that calls itself, whose arm gives that result from
# what its own lines build (Semantics ch. 4, "Binding groups and cycles": any line may use
# any name the block binds, and "the order of a group's lines decides positions and
# nothing else"; "widget functions recurse as deep as their data"; ch. 8: `<-` builds the
# child and binds its plain result, and a widget application is transparent; ruling TC).
# Nothing here is a cycle. Reaches `ArmRowOf`'s two refusals on keep-B.
# Written by Claude (sweep-4, the prismc run), 12 November 2026; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

@Wide: fn Nat -> @Nat
fn @Wide 3:
    Ui.Label($text=$"three")
    @ 1
fn @Wide k:
    @ 2

@Count: fn Nat -> @Nat
fn @Count d:
    match d -? 1:
        ? less:
            Ui.Label($text=$"level {d}")
            v <- @Count less
            @ v + 1
        nil: @ 1

@main: @unit
@main:
    w <- @Wide n                                                       # 0
    Ui.Label($text=$"wide {w}")                                        # 1
    n <- @Count 2                                                      # 2, 3
